About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

As part of the Global Operations Centre (GOC) , you will work closely with teams across the United States, Europe, and Asia to deliver high-impact solutions in a collaborative, multicultural environment. We are looking for a Junior Media Orchestrator who will: &nbsp;

• End-to-End Campaign Delivery &amp; Coordination &nbsp;
Manage campaign workflows from brief interpretation to post-campaign analysis while leading status calls, managing timelines, and keeping deliverables aligned across teams. &nbsp;

• DCO Tech Build &amp; Configuration &nbsp;
Configure, build, and maintain dynamic creative decision trees in DCO platforms to ensure audience, message, creative, and media rules execute accurately against strategy. &nbsp;

• Troubleshooting &amp; Performance Reporting &nbsp;
Identify and resolve technical, campaign, or creative issues promptly, while creating performance reports to extract actionable creative insights for optimization. &nbsp;

• New Business &amp; Market Enablement &nbsp;
Support pitches and market adoption by creating compelling case studies, workshop materials, and pitch collateral that highlight HVCS capabilities and success stories. &nbsp;

• Workflow Optimization &amp; AI Innovation &nbsp;
Leverage AI tools (such as WPP Open) and emerging DCO technologies to streamline production processes, reduce manual effort, and drive continuous workflow improvement. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Skills and Experience &nbsp;

• 2+ years' experience in Ad Operations, Digital Activation, Campaign Management or DCO platforms such as: Flashtalking/Innovid, Smartly, Celtra, etc. &nbsp;

• Advanced level of English (this will be assessed during the interview process) &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree &nbsp;

• Proven understanding of digital media channels and campaign delivery fundamentals, with hands-on experience using ad-serving and trafficking platforms. &nbsp;

• Comfortable working with campaign data, building performance reports, and applying str ong analytical skills to solve delivery challenges. &nbsp;

• Highly organized with sharp attention to detail, strong process management skills, and clear verbal and written communication. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Life at WPP Media &amp; Benefits &nbsp;

Our passion for shaping the next era of media is powered by our commitment to   Be Extraordinary, investing in our employees to inspire transformational creativity. We also   Lead Optimistically, firmly believing in and   Championing Growth and Development   for every individual. This commitment allows WPP Media employees to leverage the extensive global WPP Media &amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, build vital professional connections, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. &nbsp; &nbsp;

We   Create an Open environment   built on trust and respect, where everyone feels they belong and has opportunities to progress. This inclusive culture is fostered through a variety of employee resource groups and frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events. Our comprehensive benefits package reflects this commitment, including competitive medical, group retirement plans, vision, and dental insurance, significant paid time off, preferential partner discounts, and employee mental

About the role

We, the R&amp;D Department Humanoids at Agile Robots SE, are seeking driven Engineering Students as working Students or Interns (at least for six months) with proven hands-on experience, preferably in the field of robotics. You will support the mechanical engineers in the humanoid R&amp;D department in developing real-world, high-DOF humanoid robotic systems. We are searching for on-site support in our lab in Munich for multiple fields and focus areas like gripper/hand development, system identification, control application, and hardware design. &nbsp;

We are thrilled to know which of these topics you find most interesting to work on. Please make sure to specify and explain your favorite topic in your application

Your Responsibilities

• Create concepts and prototypes using rapid Prototyping methods (e.g., 3D printing)&nbsp;

• Development of new or existing prototype iterations to reach production level (CAD models, technical drawings, and assembly documentation)

• Assembly of prototypes and humanoid robot sub-assemblies &nbsp;

• Investigating the behavior of prototypes and assemblies to assess and meet performance and durability requirements(using virtual environments (FEM, MuJoCo), or available physical systems)

• Research State of the Art for relevant topics

