The Role&nbsp;&nbsp;

We have an opportunity for an Engineer in our AI &amp; Algorithms team, working with a particular focus on our defence and security clients. You’ll join a team of talented engineers and scientists designing, building and testing intelligent systems that solve hard, real-world problems, such as signal processing (sensor data, radar), vision, and information processing (transformers, edge AI).

As an AI Engineer, you’ll take the technical lead on parts of our projects, mentor more junior colleagues, and play an active part in shaping and winning new work. With well-equipped labs and substantial computing resources behind you, you’ll turn state-of-the-art research into systems our clients can depend on.&nbsp;

Much of our defence and security work requires security clearance, so we ask for it up front. You won’t work exclusively in that sector, but a genuine interest in it matters to us. Some examples of the projects we do can be found here .

We&nbsp;offer a flexible approach to hybrid working, although some of the projects you will be working on will require&nbsp;full-time working in the office.

What you’ll be doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Applying data-driven software development in machine learning/AI, applied statistics, and sensor processing, alongside mathematical computing techniques such as digital signal processing, simulation, and numerical optimisation.

• Taking technical ownership of significant parts of client projects, delivering quality work to budget and schedule with little supervision.&nbsp;

• Acting as technical authority or technical lead on smaller projects and contributin

We think that community engagement and communications is a critically important part of our work, and though it’s not everything , it’s close.
We’re looking for someone who loves the creative side of community engagement and communications (writing posts and press releases, creating compelling multi-media content, dreaming up creative campaigns that inspire people and invite engagement), along with the event organizer side helping create and facilitate great and impactful events, mostly dynamic, fun, engaging online events, along with the disciplined data-driven side of communications and engagement, working with the UX (user experience) and M&E (monitoring & evaluation) Lead to assess, understand, and improve our approaches to community engagement.
For the Creative Side:

• A love of writing, especially compelling creative writing for short posts, long posts, and story-telling (a love of poetry is a plus!);

• Overseeing production of multimedia content, and working with video producers and designers to realize great creative productions;

• Basic comfort using design tools, to adjust and implement design templates created by our design team;

• Fluency in creating content in English and Arabic, and French a big plus.

For the Event Organizer Side:

• Experience designing and implementing meticulous detailed-oriented events, including both offline and online events;

• Comfort using and facilitating events with online event platforms;

• Enthusiasm about working with a broad ecosystem of partners, and designing collaborative events that delight our partners as much as the attendees;

• Experience in tech, startup, and social innovation events a plus.

For the Disciplined Data-Driven Side:

• Posting content on social media platforms, and comfort with running multiple tests of content to continually learn and optimize content and approaches;

• Demonstrated experience with segmenting users and content testing;

• Experience using monitoring and analytics tools for creating detailed communications impact reports.

• Part-time ok to start (minimum 3-4 days/week availability), with preference towards full-time availability in the near future

• Remote work / partial remote work is ok (some presence in Lebanon is a plus, but not required)

• Initial contract is as a “consultant/contractor”, with potential for shifting to a full-time position in the future

• Benefits (health care, pension, vacation accrual, etc) are available once people shift to full-time positions

