About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

YOUR ROLE IN A NUTSHELL

The Production Coordinator is embedded in WPP Production's Sydney-based primary production team. &nbsp;

The Production Coordinator is an entry level role providing a great professional opportunity to build competence in all facets of advertising and marketing content projects, including but not limited to integrated communications, motion, photography, ecom, social, OOH, and digital production. &nbsp;

As a Production Coordinator, you support more senior members of the Production team to execute their projects that deliver over and beyond, and that add real value to our client and agency partners. You also have hands-on input into smaller scale projects, contributing from start to delivery, with guidance from more senior Producers. &nbsp;

The Production Coordinator is responsible for contributing to day to day production workflows and processes - building awareness on the how and why that the workflows are adhered to, defined, and communicated, with a focus on administrative tasks across production and finance systems. &nbsp;

With an understanding of content and advertising production processes, you will be motivated, results orientated and be confident in using good judgement in all decisions and actions and is committed to delivering on all tasks that have been delegated to you. &nbsp;

Working with a team of industry experts, the role represents a great opportunity for an aspiring production assistant or coordinator to gain hands-on experience in a fast moving creative environment, with exposure to experienced mentors. &nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL DO

You'll be responsible for supporting the Producer Team in relation to project documentation, including creation of supplier records, purchase orders, estimates, project schedules and resourcing, as well as co-ordinating Material Instructions for all projects across the team. &nbsp;

You'll have direct exposure to small and medium-sized productions across all forms of media including tv commercials, social, print and digital; with production knowledge at a beginner level, you'll be able to understand and interpret technical production terminology, techniques, and processes. &nbsp;

In terms of process support, you'll respond in a timely fashion to requests from internal and external stakeholders in regards to all aspects of project delivery (costs, timings, quality of output, change requests, risks, etc.) &nbsp;

ABOUT YOU

• Ideally some exposure to or experience in agency or studio environments that produce advertising content, content marketing, or a related field, with a strong depth of proficiency across various forms of media (marketing content, photography, integrated communications, post, social, OOH).

